   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region, so I have not checked it against any external source.\n\n**Peptide chain, left to right**\n- N-acetyl group (CH3C(=O)NH\u2013) on an indan-2-yl glycine residue.\n- 4-Chlorophenylalanine.\n- Lysine, with the free NH2 on a four-carbon chain.\n- Leucine (isobutyl side chain), whose C-terminal amide is attached to a para-substituted aniline.\n\n**Stereochemistry from wedges and hashes**\n- Working through each wedge or hash gives S for the indanylglycine alpha carbon (N[C@@H](indanyl)C(=O)).\n- The Phe, Lys and Leu alpha carbons come out as the natural L-configuration (N[C@@H](side chain)C(=O)).\n- The vinyl group is drawn trans (E), so I wrote it with `/C=C/`.\n- The spiro dioxetane carbons and the adamantane carbons have no wedges or hashes, so they carry no stereo marks.\n\n**Right-hand side**\n- The aniline ring carries a CH2\u2013O\u2013aryl (benzyl ether) group at the para position.\n- The aryl ring has the ether oxygen on one carbon.\n- Next to the oxygen carbon is a chlorine-bearing carbon, then a carbon bearing the dioxetane.\n- The dioxetane carries an OMe and is spiro-fused to adamantane at the 2-position.\n- On the other side of the oxygen-bearing carbon, the ring carries the trans CH=CH\u2013C\u2261N group.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@@H](C1Cc2ccccc2C1)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(Cl)cc1)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)Nc1ccc(COc2c(Cl)c(C3(OC)OOC34C5CC6CC(C5)CC4C6)ccc2/C=C/C#N)cc1"
